// =============================================================================
// 04_identity_match_rate.kql  |  Label: [NET-NEW]
//
// Pain #3 (FLAGSHIP) — MEASURE THE MATCH RATE, throttle-safe.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
//   01_identity_join.kql PROVES the join returns rows. It does NOT quantify how
//   MANY gateway queries actually got an owner — the one number the repo cannot
//   produce without a live tenant (phase5 U11 / U19; PAIN-POINT-COVERAGE.md #3).
//   This file computes: (# gateway queries with ExecutingUser) / (# gateway
//   queries in the window) = the attribution match rate, broken down by
//   QueryType so DirectQuery-vs-Refresh coverage is visible separately (the
//   open question in 01_identity_join.kql's header).
//
// THROTTLE-SAFE BY CONSTRUCTION (Session 1/3 blocker: trial Spark/KQL throttle)
//   Every block below pushes `lookback` + `workspace_filter` down BEFORE the join,
//   exactly like 01_identity_join.kql, so a throttled trial capacity scans a tiny
//   slice. Start at 15m + a single workspace GUID; widen only once it returns.
//   On F2+ you can set lookback = 24h and empty the workspace filter.
//
// PREREQUISITES (same as 01_identity_join.kql — all must hold or match rate = 0
// for a boring reason, not a real miss):
//   - Workspace Monitoring ON for the workspace(s) whose models refresh through
//     the gateway, and its Eventhouse actually provisioned (blocked on trial —
//     see LIVE-TENANT-FINDINGS.md 2026-07-02; needs F2+).
//   - Gateway QueryExecution logs landed into THIS Eventhouse as
//     bronze_query_execution (via 01_bronze_ingest.py) OR reachable via a OneLake
//     shortcut / externaldata. Without the gateway side there is no denominator.
//   - At least one real gateway-routed refresh/query in the window.
//
// HOW TO READ THE RESULT
//   match_rate_pct is the flagship number. Report it in the pilot issue
//   (field "Attribution match rate (U11)"). Also report the per-QueryType split:
//   Refresh is expected high; DirectQuery is the genuinely-unknown case.
// =============================================================================

// ---- tunables (identical semantics to 01_identity_join.kql) -----------------
let lookback = 15m;                    // START here on a throttled trial; widen on F2+
let workspace_filter = dynamic([]);    // e.g. dynamic(["<workspace-guid>"]) under throttle

// ---- gateway side (denominator): every gateway query in the window ----------
let gw =
    bronze_query_execution
    | where QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC > ago(lookback)
    | project RequestId, QueryType, GatewayObjectId,
              QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC;

// ---- monitoring side: identities available in the window --------------------
let ids =
    PowerBIDatasetsWorkspace
    | where Timestamp > ago(lookback)
    | where array_length(workspace_filter) == 0 or WorkspaceId in (workspace_filter)
    | where OperationName in ("QueryEnd", "ExecutionMetrics", "RefreshEnd")
    | project OperationId, ExecutingUser, ItemName;

// =============================================================================
// BLOCK A — HEADLINE MATCH RATE (the one number)
// =============================================================================
gw
| join kind=leftouter ids on $left.RequestId == $right.OperationId
| summarize
    total_gateway_queries   = count(),
    attributed_queries      = countif(isnotempty(ExecutingUser)),
    distinct_users          = dcountif(ExecutingUser, isnotempty(ExecutingUser)),
    distinct_datasets       = dcountif(ItemName, isnotempty(ItemName))
| extend match_rate_pct = round(100.0 * attributed_queries / total_gateway_queries, 1)
| project total_gateway_queries, attributed_queries, match_rate_pct,
          distinct_users, distinct_datasets

// =============================================================================
// BLOCK B — MATCH RATE BY QUERY TYPE (Refresh vs DirectQuery = the open question)
// Run separately: comment out Block A, uncomment below.
// =============================================================================
// gw
// | join kind=leftouter ids on $left.RequestId == $right.OperationId
// | summarize
//     total     = count(),
//     attributed = countif(isnotempty(ExecutingUser))
//     by QueryType
// | extend match_rate_pct = round(100.0 * attributed / total, 1)
// | order by total desc

// =============================================================================
// BLOCK C — UNATTRIBUTED SAMPLE (diagnose misses)
// The gateway queries that got NO owner. If this is large, check: is Workspace
// Monitoring on the RIGHT workspace? Is the window wide enough to contain the
// monitoring row (engine event can land minutes after the gateway row)? Is the
// query a Dataflow Gen1 / Paginated Report (confirmed-not-covered)?
// Run separately: comment out Block A, uncomment below.
// =============================================================================
// gw
// | join kind=leftouter ids on $left.RequestId == $right.OperationId
// | where isempty(ExecutingUser)
// | project QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC, RequestId, QueryType, GatewayObjectId
// | order by QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC desc
// | take 25
